{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cream-capitate-snake","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nThe one confirmed ungated representation mirror (12a Part 1): `scripts/gen_api_surface.py` + `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` gate the library's public surface, and `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` generates docs from the MCP registrar — but nothing cross-checks the MCP tool surface against the library facade, so the two can drift silently (the S1 sample's live example: MCP tool signatures diverging from the library surface). Precedent: Kubernetes `hack/verify-generated.sh` (regen-in-isolated-worktree + diff); the repo's own generated-registry pattern.\n\n## Approach\n\nIntrospect the MCP registrar's tool inventory (names, parameters, defaults) and the library facade functions they wrap; emit a normalized parity manifest; a `--check` mode diffs against the committed manifest and fails on divergence, wired into `make lint`. Regeneration documented in the script's --help. Where a tool intentionally diverges from the facade (e.g., enumerated MCP params vs **fields passthrough — the known edit_ticket case), the manifest records the divergence explicitly so drift is still caught relative to the declared shape.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: a script produces a normalized MCP↔library parity manifest and `--check` fails (exit != 0) when either side drifts from the committed manifest.\n- [ ] AC2: `make lint` runs the check; a seeded mismatch (test fixture) proves it fires RED.\n- [ ] AC3: intentional divergences are declared in the manifest with a reason field, and an undeclared divergence still fails.\n- [ ] AC4: regeneration is one documented command; docs updated where the sibling generators are documented.\n\n## File impact\n\n- scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py (new; or extend gen_api_surface.py — decide at implementation against the existing script's structure)\n- tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py (new)\n- Makefile (lint target wiring)\n- docs/mcp-reference.md or docs/reuse-surface.md (regeneration note)","id":"8ce5-b870-601d-4715","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"MCP-tool-surface vs library-facade parity gate"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788311488040258364,"uuid":"23452547-6c56-47cd-88b4-d159827b8acd"}